  (uuid_generate_v4(), 'signed-authentic-native-american-indian-jewelry-kingman-turquoise-navajo-humming', '4606470367', 'https://www.etsy.com/listing/4606470367/signed-authentic-native-american-indian?click_key=EuF0FihyIEpKRoa5cd1jahRJH-99%3ALT710abaf834c3b61c0e682473a6a3f797d1587944&click_sum=f1be7d33&ls=a&ga_order=most_relevant&ga_search_type=all&ga_view_type=gallery&ga_search_query=Navajo+jewelry&ref=search_grid-455539-20-3&sr_prefetch=1&pf_from=search&pro=1&frs=1&cns=1&sts=1',
   'SIGNED Authentic Native American Indian Jewelry Kingman Turquoise Navajo Hummingbird Brooch Pin Sterling Silver Southwestern', 'SIGNED Authentic Native American Navajo Zuni Sleeping Beauty Sterling Silver Hummingbird Brooch or Pin. This Beautiful Exquisitely Handcrafted Hummingbird measures 2.5” in length and measures 1 5/8” wide. It features a gemstone of Kingman Turquoise in Sterling Silver. Just amazing and Perfect for Hummingbird Lovers. Stamped Sterling Silver and Handcrafted by Navajo Artist ❤️ R. Sellers The Hummingbird represents a physical form of a spirit helper and guide. The meaning of the Hummingbird symbol is peace, love, and happiness. Native American Indians are a deeply spiritual people and they communicate their history, thoughts, ideas and dreams from generation to generation through Symbols and Signs such as the Hummingbird symbol. Native American bird and animal symbols and totems are believed to represent the physical form of a spirit helper and guide. The meaning of the Hummingbird symbol is to signify peace, love and happiness. Hummingbirds are also admired as ferocious fighters and defenders of their territory. Native Americans believe that it brings luck to see a Hummingbird before major events such as long hunting trips or travelling to other villages. Hummingbird feathers are highly prized and used ceremonially and in dance costumes.', 'turquoise-jewelry',
